isGenSegment -- gen-segment ideals
**********************************

  * Usage: 
        isGenSegment J
  * Inputs:
      * J, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, or
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a strongly stable ideal.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, 

Description
===========

The first element of the sequence is a boolean value. It tells if the ideal is
a segment, i.e. if there exists a term ordering such that every generator of
the ideal is strictly greater than every monomial outside the ideal of the same
degree. If true, the second element of the sequence contains the list of
weights giving the corresponding ordering on the monomials.



+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[x,y,z];                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : isGenSegment(ideal(x^2,x*y,y^4))  |
|                                       |
|o2 = (true, {6, 3, 1})                 |
|                                       |
|o2 : Sequence                          |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : isGenSegment(ideal(x^2,x*y^3,y^4))|
|                                       |
|o3 = (true, {4, 3, 1})                 |
|                                       |
|o3 : Sequence                          |
+---------------------------------------+

