isHilbertPolynomial -- Determine whether a numerical polynomial can be a Hilbert polynomial
*******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isHilbertPolynomial p
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note projective Hilbert polynomial:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,, or
      * p, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a numerical
        univariate polynomial.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Returns true if the input polynomial is an admissible Hilbert polynomial, false
otherwise.



+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[t];                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isHilbertPolynomial(3*t+4)                              |
|                                                             |
|o2 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isHilbertPolynomial((2/3)*t-1)                          |
|                                                             |
|o3 = false                                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isHilbertPolynomial(2*projectiveHilbertPolynomial(2))   |
|                                                             |
|o4 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isHilbertPolynomial(2*projectiveHilbertPolynomial(2,-1))|
|                                                             |
|o5 = false                                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

