lexIdeal -- Compute the saturated lexicographic ideal in the given ambient space with given Hilbert polynomial
**************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        lexIdeal (hp ,S)
        lexIdeal (hp, n)
        lexIdeal (d, S)
        lexIdeal (d, n)
  * Inputs:
      * hp, a *note projective Hilbert polynomial:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,, or
      * hp, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a Hilbert
        polynomial;
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a positive integer
        corresponding to a constant Hilbert polynomial;
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, with numgens
        S > 1;
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of variables of the
        polynomial ring.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing:
        lexIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value QQ, Option to set the ring of coefficients
      * *note OrderVariables: lexIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOrderVariables=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value Down, Option to set the order of indexed
        variables
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

Returns the saturated lexicographic ideal defining a subscheme of
\mathbb{P}^{n} or Proj S with Hilbert polynomial hp or d.



+--------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[t];                     |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : S = QQ[x,y,z,w];           |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : lexIdeal(4*t, S)           |
|                                |
|                5   4 2         |
|o3 = ideal (x, y , y z )        |
|                                |
|o3 : Ideal of S                 |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : lexIdeal(4*t, 5)           |
|                                |
|                     5   4 2    |
|o4 = ideal (x , x , x , x x )   |
|             1   0   2   2 3    |
|                                |
|o4 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]        |
|                  0   4         |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : hp = hilbertPolynomial oo  |
|                                |
|o5 = - 4*P  + 4*P               |
|          0      1              |
|                                |
|o5 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial|
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : lexIdeal(hp, S)            |
|                                |
|                5   4 2         |
